					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403201#post-2670194</guid>
				<title>Random Article Review #7, 13 October 2016</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-403201/scp-803#post-2670194</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 13 Oct 2016 19:02:28 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Kalinin</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2203795</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I think there was probably more of an appetite for body horror in 2011, which along with the strangeness of animate surgery umbrellas is the main draw. In a lot of ways, the context of the site at the time matters for this one. Back then, there were about a thousand fewer articles, and maybe not quite so many articles to have to stand above when it came to the &quot;is this strange enough&quot; and &quot;is this gory enough&quot; thresholds. As a reader in 2016, I'm not really feeling much.</p> <p>This article suffers from a severe overuse of redaction. There are numerous gratuitous &quot;[DATA EXPUNGED]&quot; uses, stuff like censoring of percentages which doesn't really make a whole lot of sense when you think about it, and censoring the fate of the expendable D-Class when there's no real reason they wouldn't just write &quot;and then he blew up.&quot; I'm not really moved conceptually, but tightening up that part of affairs would make this a lot more readable.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
